cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this formalization, please cite the specific archived version you checked, not
  the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI; see the "Archival" section
  in README.md.
title: >-
  minimal-uniformity-lean: Lean 4 formalization of the pen-and-paper core of "Minimal
  uniformity of the non-Archimedean vertex types in unit-edge tilings"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the human-checked mathematics that sharpens the
  exhaustive scans behind the paper's lower bounds: the chamber bound, the rigidity of the
  class and its forced irregular corner, the corner-orbit lemma, the permanence of word
  violations under refinement, and the lattice and Euler counts that close the (3^2.6^2) case
  in both categories. The scans themselves are certificate-backed elsewhere and are not the
  target here. Every result is sorry-free and native_decide-free, depending at most on
  propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound; the corner-orbit lemmas depend on no axioms at
  all. The toolchain is pinned by lean-toolchain and lake-manifest.json, so lake exe cache get
  && lake build reproduces the checked build.
type: software
